"""
Physics-informed CRAB/OC optimizer for 1Q transmon X90/Y90 gates.

This is a self-contained replacement for the previous arbitrary 4K CRAB search.
It keeps RB as the only optimizer/checkpoint experiment: no leakage RB and no
purity RB are run here.

Main idea
---------
Instead of allowing independent arbitrary I/Q corrections for X90 and Y90, this
optimizes a low-dimensional, interpretable correction basis:

    x[0]  amplitude correction
    x[1]  DRAG / derivative-quadrature correction
    x[2]  constant pulse-axis phase correction
    x[3]  intra-pulse phase ramp, detuning-like
    x[4:] small windowed complex tones near |alpha| ~ 100 MHz

The Y90 correction is generated as a 90-degree I/Q rotation of the X90
correction, which greatly reduces the dimension and makes the search less able
to exploit fast-RB noise.

Assumptions
-----------
- Existing config contains X90_wf_<q>, X90_wf_der_<q>, Y90_wf_<q>,
  Y90_wf_der_<q> waveforms, matching your original conventions.
- RB1Q_CRAB accepts a supplied config and has .gate_fidelity(), .data,
  .iname, .fname attributes as in your previous script.
- The OPX sample clock is 1 ns/sample for the generated arbitrary waveforms.

Things to tune first
--------------------
- QUBIT
- LEAK_FREQS_MHZ
- FAST_CIRCUIT_DEPTHS
- NUM_CIRCUITS_FAST / SHOTS_FAST
- Bounds in decode_physical_params()

No leakage RB or purity RB is called anywhere in this file.
"""

